  </sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Thrill Seekers" id="3e41-919c-e639-f8bf" hidden="false">
      <description>If your Army Faction is EMPERORS CHILDREN:
  -&gt; Ranged weapons equipped by models in this unit gain [ASSAULT].
  -&gt; The unit is eligible to declare a charge in a turn in which it Advanced.
  -&gt; The unit is eligible to shoot in a turn in which it Fell Back.
  -&gt; The unit is eligible to declare a charge in a turn in which it Fell Back.
  If the unit advanced this turn or if the unit fell back this turn:
    -&gt; The unit cannot target enemy units with ranged attacks if the target unit was engaged with this unit at the start of the turn.
    -&gt; The unit cannot target enemy units with a charge if the target unit was engaged with this unit at the start of the turn.
  If the unit advanced this turn or if the unit fell back this turn:
    -&gt; The unit cannot target enemy units with ranged attacks if a unit other than this unit has selected the target unit as a target this phase or a unit other than this unit has selected the target unit as a charge target this phase.
    -&gt; The unit cannot target enemy units with a charge if a unit other than this unit has selected the target unit as a target this phase or a unit other than this unit has selected the target unit as a charge target this phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Pact of Excess" id="2ec9-1af5-cacd-4db7" hidden="false">
      <description>You cannot select Legions of Excess as your Army Faction.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
